<description>&lt;p&gt;Iranian drones struck a Komala base in Erbil with no casualties, while Iran intensified attacks on Kurdish opposition groups in northern Iraq and a militia leader publicly criticized Iraq's stance on the Iran blockade. Iraqi security forces captured a notorious ISIS gang member in Kirkuk and arrested suspects for usury in Wasit, embezzlement in Mosul and defamation in Najaf, and foiled petroleum-product smuggling in territorial waters. A Jewish heritage museum opened in Baghdad and Iran exempted ships from India and three other nations from Strait of Hormuz transit restrictions. The UCDP recorded 396 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMihAFBVV95cUxPckpWSVBWREltTGMxckdQTzROOXdyVEQzQTJQUXZvMGhxcnlEWExZUVNyT3AxN1hpN1Jjal9aeDVpQ1BkbDNYdlM0OHlVcndQUjBibUh3TE13anRrZGp3anVOSXU3VE1Yc2FHYTBjUVJlclkzUUFkdF8xNWp2d1BGY1ZjbDc?oc=5&quot;&gt;Institute for the Study of War&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMilgFBVV95cUxNVEpsYkFObUtiNHFxbHRpek00YWdINGl1QjdYRG1mZVRsRkxuVThKcExXOUlHRjQxMFZEM28wUUR4ekVRRGY1dDdNUGhkZUxGb2tvMi1ScXB3c0N2bTQ0NE9PdnZ6Y0hHendhdEoySkFNclZ1MC1BTmlyUDY0X1VHNTZnV0w2ZEZaOC1KYVFFSUhXbTRmdkE?oc=5&quot;&gt;Kurdistan24&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiZkFVX3lxTE5tXzRMZi1nWDJuZWlHTGVoRTI3cjNpMzlXNGdqZWxIMVFIQTZqTkVDUG40NEV2TXM1MEVZYlkxYkcybmVKd0NUTXlpUzhzcWx0dUNXZDVEXzdPWld1Qm1HMVo3dmE3QQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Soufan Center&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMitAFBVV95cUxOZmZJbVhyYWJqZGRRT0s4U2VMVGUzeHpYc0JoYXdKWEszUWptbHdHenlCWmxSWWp6ekdkRV81ZzVhV2lEY3pGVm9FTXY5RG9HMnoydGRyLWEyY2JreW9acHc2RDFqYklPM2hWZEl3OGRURlQydFZ4V1BXYWVmMVFpWnU5OEZPLVZaTW5wdVR6RkpUbWpZMUVJNU9KbF84LTA5bjV4YjVwRFlvMExndmNiQ2VlazE?oc=5&quot;&gt;MEMRI | Middle East Media Rese